# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 sym2poly.cc algnum_normal and algnum_rewritable, the primitive-element path of normal and simplify for expressions with algebraic numbers. (1) When the expression E satisfies a biquadratic, algnum_rewritable writes it as shift+e or shift-e with e=sqrt(sol) and took the minus sign whenever is_positive(E-shift) was false, which it is for every complex E-shift: normal(sqrt(2)+i*sqrt(3)) gave -sqrt(2)*(1+i*2*sqrt(6)/4) (the negation), also simplify(exp(i*pi/6)*sqrt(2)), normal((-8)^(1/6)), det([[sqrt(2),-sqrt(3)],[i,1]]) and normal(sqrt(-sqrt(2))) = -sqrt(-sqrt(2)). Now the sign whose value (evalf at extpar.digits) is nearer E-shift is taken; a root with no numeric value keeps the real test. (2) With a rootof among the radicals (a cube root after patch 0045), algnum_normal writes the generator as rootof([1,0],pminv), which alg_evalf reads as the root with the largest real part, while the generator's value r may be another root of pminv: normal(sqrt(10^(1/3)-sqrt(6))) was a degree-12 rootof worth 2.1457 (right 0.5432*i). Giac's own RUR branch (#else) checks that r is that root; now the active branch does the same at 100 digits, and a generator that is not the rootof keeps the radicals.
